# M4 touch-plate LED registers: L<ctrl>.<k> brightness + R<ctrl>.<k> colour
# (manual/hardware.md §6.11 "The LEDs" / "Registers", issue #80).
#
#   "The LED below the touch plates can be accessed with an L register - just
#    like in the P2B8. In addition, there is a R register that controls the
#    color of the LED, similar to those on the master. If you just use the R
#    registers, the LED will light in full brightness. If you just use the L
#    register, the LED lights white in the brightness specified by the value you
#    feed into that register. Using both R and L at the same time gives you
#    control over brightness and color."
#
# The M4 is the ONLY controller with R registers (Forge numControllerRegisters:
# only m4 declares REGISTER_RGB_LED). "Just use R" / "just use L" is a property
# of the PATCH, not of the tick: the engine decides per fader from the static
# bindings (Engine::registerDriven), so an L-only fader stays white even on a
# tick where the driving circuit happens to write 0.
#
# Readback: `F<n>.led` is FaderState.led (brightness 0..1), `F<n>.color` is
# FaderState.ledColor (a DROID colour value; negative == the white sentinel
# SeqCore::kLedWhite, 0 == dark per basics.md §5.5).
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]

# Fader 1: R only, and LIVE off an input -- full brightness, colour follows CV.
[copy]
    input = I1
    output = R1.1

# Fader 2: L only -> white at the given brightness.
[copy]
    input = 0.5
    output = L1.2

# Fader 3: both -> the R hue at the L brightness.
[copy]
    input = 0.5
    output = L1.3
[copy]
    input = 0.4
    output = R1.3

# Fader 4: R only, value 0 -> dark (the renderer maps colour 0 to black).
[copy]
    input = 0
    output = R1.4
>>>
# R only: brightness pinned at 1, colour = the R value.
@0 set I1 0.8
@0 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@0 expect F1.color 0.8 tol 1e-6
# L only: white sentinel, brightness = the L value.
@0 expect F2.led 0.5 tol 1e-6
@0 expect F2.color -1 tol 1e-6
# Both: hue at brightness.
@0 expect F3.led 0.5 tol 1e-6
@0 expect F3.color 0.4 tol 1e-6
# R = 0.0 -> dark, still at full brightness (the colour, not the level, is off).
@0 expect F4.led 1 tol 1e-6
@0 expect F4.color 0 tol 1e-6
#
# Live: the R register is an ordinary register write, so the plate follows it
# every tick.
@1 set I1 0.4
@1 expect F1.color 0.4 tol 1e-6
@1 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
# An R-only fader driven to 0 goes dark and comes back -- it never falls back to
# white, because the patch does not drive L1.1.
@2 set I1 0
@2 expect F1.color 0 tol 1e-6
@2 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@3 set I1 1.1
@3 expect F1.color 1.1 tol 1e-6
